Z||000000||fotofrank||04-02-2000||11:31 AM||||I belive I fixed the temp gauge "stick" problem. i was doing some work on my instument pod and checked the temp gauge needle stick on start problem. it seems the needle hits the instrument pod bezel. You know that metle pice with the red/orange collor back. I used my small hand held grinder and shaved down the area that the needle hit. No stick. Be carefull to not take off too much. No wires need be cut and spliced. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000001||theogre||04-02-2000||05:18 PM||||The reason we do the wiring change is to correct the function of the gauge. The gauge is not suposed to swing up like that in the first place. Instead the temp light is suposed to light. Basically GM or one of it's contractors got the color code backwards for the 2 wires.<P>Contrary to the belief of some you don't have to take the whole dash apart to fix it.<P>1 drop the lower dash trim.<BR>2 loosen the 4 steering column bolts/nuts that hold the bracket to the dash. Remove the front right nut.<BR>3 remove the back cover of the dash.<BR>4 follow the rest of the fix as described by others for the wires.<P>total fix time is less than 1 hour. I did mine one day on my lunch break. Did it with no cutting of the harness at all and the addition of one wire and teminal. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 04-02-2000).]||||reg||1
